  "instructions": [
    "Combine the rice, 3 cups water, and 1/4 tsp of the salt in a saucepan. Bring to a boil, cover, and cook on low for 15 minutes until the water is absorbed.",
    "Toss the sliced beef with 1 tbsp cornstarch in a bowl until lightly coated.",
    "Whisk the coconut aminos, 1/2 cup water, ginger, 1 tsp cornstarch, and maple syrup in a small bowl.",
    "Heat 1 tbsp oil in a 12-inch skillet over medium-high heat. Add half the beef in a single layer and cook 2 minutes per side until browned. Move to a plate and repeat with 1 tbsp oil and the remaining beef.",
    "Add the last 1 tbsp oil to the skillet. Add the broccoli, the remaining salt, and 2 tbsp water from the sauce bowl's measure if the pan looks dry, then cook 4 minutes until bright green and just tender.",
    "Add the garlic and stir for 30 seconds until fragrant.",
    "Return the beef to the pan and pour in the sauce. Stir for 2 minutes until the sauce thickens and the beef reaches 145 F.",
    "Fluff the rice with a fork and serve the beef and broccoli over it."
  ],
